--- A list no line of the program gives an item holds no value ever: a
--- loop over it runs no rounds, so a loop over one of its items is never
--- reached either — `for t in row` of `for row in e`, `e = []` never
--- pushed onto, prints nothing and the program goes on, in both modes. It
--- had been refused ("'row' is an item of a list never given one, so it
--- has no kind to walk"), since the compiled program, holding the item as
--- text, did not build (Rosetta Code, Tropical algebra overloading; errors
--- k08 until 2026-11-08).
e = []
for row in e
    for t in row
        log[t]
log['done']

--- (a function handed an empty matrix walks its rows and each row's
--- numbers: none)
fn doubled[m]
    out = []
    for row in m
        for x in row
            out = push[out, x * 2]
    len[out]

log[doubled[[]]]

--- (and a collecting loop over such a list is the list of no items)
names = for row in e
    for t in row
        log[t]
    len[row]
log[names]

--- (so is one over `[]` written as its list: the compiled program names
--- the literal's items ints, as a statement loop's — `vec![]` alone had
--- named no type, and the program did not build; crow check --self's
--- shape/collect/empty)
got = for x in []
    x
log[got]
